<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03K1">Corollary <span data-tag="03K1">8.1.2.11</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category. For every pair of objects $X,Y \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the coslice inclusion $\iota _{X}$ restricts to a homotopy equivalence of Kan complexes </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}^{\mathrm{L}}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(X,Y) \hookrightarrow \{ X\}  \times _{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} } \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \{ Y\} . \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Proposition <a data-tag="03K0" href="/tag/03K0">8.1.2.10</a> with Corollary <a data-tag="01VE" href="/tag/01VE">5.1.6.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
